<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>x500_2m</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>
  <author>
    <name>Benjamin Perseghetti</name>
    <email>bperseghetti@rudislabs.com</email>
  </author>
  <description>Model of the NXP HoverGames Drone development kit (KIT-HGDRONEK66), uniformly rescaled from the base X500 so the diagonal motor-to-motor distance spans 2 m. Reuses the mesh/material/license assets from the x500_15m model directory; only the geometric scale here differs. Mass, yaw inertia (izz), and motor plugin constants are unchanged from the real X500. Roll/pitch inertia (ixx/iyy) is scaled up by the arm-length ratio (4.0638x) versus the real X500 so the roll/pitch torque-to-inertia ratio -- and therefore PX4's default attitude/position-hold gains -- still match the real vehicle despite the longer arms; without this the vehicle underdamps and oscillates in the horizontal plane while holding a fixed setpoint.</description>
</model>
